description: "guarantees[5]: Explainable Reasoning,Traceable Thinking,Memory Integration,Graph Execution,Deterministic Reconstruction"
spec:
  id: cognitive_graph
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Cognition
  compiler_stage: Cognitive Representation
  description: "\"Defines the Universal Cognitive Graph (UCG), the execution model of engineering reasoning. A Cognitive Graph represents thought as a directed, composable graph of cognitive operations connected through evidence, hypotheses, constraints, memories and decisions.\""
purpose: Represent engineering thinking as an executable graph.
examples[4]: "Example_01[9]: Observe,→,Retrieve Memory,→,Compare,→,Infer,→,Decision","Example_02[9]: Bug,→,Hypothesis A,→,Validation,→,Reject,→,Hypothesis B","Example_03[7]: Requirements,→,Architecture,→,Tradeoff,→,Decision","Example_04[7]: Performance Metric,→,Optimization,→,Benchmark,→,Reflection"
success: "\"Every engineering thought is represented as a reusable, explainable cognitive graph.\""
future:
  probabilistic_graphs: true
  graph_embeddings: true
  graph_search: true
  graph_execution_engine: true
  distributed_reasoning: true
